    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32706" root="غيد" body-key="g">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيِدَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيَدَ</span></b> , (L, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيَدٌ</span>, (L,) <i>He had
a bending neck, and limber sides:</i> (L, K:) or <i>he
had a lax,</i> or <i>limber, neck.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيِدَت</span>
is app. said of a young woman as meaning <i>She
was soft,</i> or <i>tender;</i> or <i>soft,</i> or <i>tender, and limber
in the sides.</i> (See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيَدٌ</span> below.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيِدَ</span> <i>He
was,</i> or <i>became, drowsy;</i> or <i>drowsy and with a
bending of the neck.</i> (See, again, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيَدٌ</span> below.)]

